{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794186443,"nonce":"wGwxyvfBGNA00DyoCjp+dqv4Nyk=","message":"Front end, analyzer and naga lowering in the working tree (uncommitted):\n- intern.rs (Symbol interner), types.rs (hash-consed TypeId arena with abstract int and float), hir.rs (per-body arenas for exprs and locals; shadowing is a new LocalId), front/ (module-scope names in any order, block scopes, attributes, struct literals by field name, glam-style constructors and casts), builtins.rs (Rust method names to naga math functions with typing rules).\n- check/: bidirectional inference with abstract literals concretised by context, operator rules (vector and scalar mixing, matrix products, comparisons to bool vectors, shifts by u32), builtin signatures, places and mutability (rustc-style messages), return paths, break/continue placement, call graph ordering with recursion rejected; rules for entry-point IO (bound, typed, unique locations, vertex position), resource bindings (unique, host-shareable, runtime arrays last), Rust naming conventions, unused variables and items, unreachable code.\n- lower/: straight to naga (WGSL layout offsets via Layouter, constants and overrides folded by ConstantEvaluator, Emit bookkeeping, mut locals and params as variables, places as pointers, while and for as naga loops with the range evaluated once, a match holding break or continue lowered to an if chain because naga's break leaves a switch).\n- Diagnostics carry spans; naga spans index the span table, so validation errors land on the Rust token. ariadne renders them in the CLI and russl_build (feature ); russl! emits compile_error! per error and a deprecated item per warning.\nTests: 11 pipeline tests (triangle and compute for every target, abstract literals, error spans by line and column, binding and recursion errors, lint warnings), 4 unit tests, 2 macro tests.\n\nStill open here: texture sampling and loads (types bind, no methods yet), uniform address-space layout (16-byte array strides; naga's validator will reject such a uniform today), array lengths from constants, multi-component swizzle assignment, f16 literals (lowered through an f32 conversion), trybuild compile-fail tests (the span checks live in tests/compile.rs for now). Note: an if used as a value lowers to select, so both branches are evaluated.","files":null}]}